        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: West Lodge, Cardiff Castle, Cardiff city centre, Cardiff Castle\n- Structures: West Gate Lodge, Animal Wall\n- Topics: Grade II* listed buildings, tea rooms, sculptured walls\n\nFacts:\n- The West Lodge, also called the West Gate Lodge, to Cardiff Castle is a Grade II* listed building in the centre of Cardiff, Wales.\n- The West Lodge is currently used as a tea room.\n- The West Lodge is about 100 metres west of Cardiff Castle.\n- The Animal Wall runs between the West Lodge and Cardiff Castle.\n- The Animal Wall, or \"Mur Anifeiliaid\" in Welsh, is a sculptured wall in the Castle Quarter of Cardiff city centre, Wales.\n- The Animal Wall depicts 15 animals.",
